      "question_text": "5 Consider the following three statements: 1 10p2 + 1 and 10p2 − 1 are both prime when p is an odd prime. 2 Every prime greater than 5 is of the form 6n + 1 for some integer n. 3 No multiple of 7 greater than 7 is prime. The result 91 = 7 × 13 can be used to provide a counterexample to which of the above statements? 8&/(6 >7XUQRYHU",
